{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01SQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$P$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$P$", "MATH_0005": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0006": "$U$", "MATH_0007": "$x$", "MATH_0008": "$X$", "MATH_0009": "$V \\subset S$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{O}_S(V) \\to \\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "MATH_0011": "$P$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-locally-P}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a0e33cf939d36e3ab3418e457ce0fd2e91f9803a17d98be6b9bf15ea4daec035", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:50431b0679fe459e994f62cfcb260cad068144545076b5fa14909e5fafde5c73", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a property of ring maps.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a morphism of schemes.\nWe say <MATH_0003> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>locally of type <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if for any <MATH_0005>\nthere exists an affine open neighbourhood <MATH_0006> of <MATH_0007>\nin <MATH_0008> which maps into an affine open <MATH_0009> such that\nthe induced ring map <MATH_0010>\nhas property <MATH_0011>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a704fec513edd780e829b40855b85d4a741811a615a2d8a817d724d3268593f9", "unit_id": "tag:01SS:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01SQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$P$", "MATH_0002": "$P$", "MATH_0003": "$P$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7bcdae5fbeef7a8fa161851fe687deebc96ed2d08853d110d2c541cca6d75492", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d98ba3eba5f86b2041f1aefd4386ab57b981c94f11357e8c0374501e801bd146", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis is not a ``good'' definition unless the property <MATH_0001> is\na local property. Even if <MATH_0002> is a local property we will not\nautomatically use this definition to say that a morphism is\n``locally of type <MATH_0003>'' unless we also explicitly state the\ndefinition elsewhere.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d3bdecaf1a718447d83277a1872823f6a0f3e8ea096932b5db698ce50df27264", "unit_id": "tag:01SQ:prose-0002"}
